# Prettier already reads .gitignore, so dist/, node_modules/ and the other
# generated trees are covered without being named here. This file is for
# tracked files Prettier must not touch.
#
# Prettier owns .ts, .tsx, .mjs, .js and the hand-written config files. That is
# the gap: eslint.config.js extends no stylistic preset, so before this nothing
# looked at whitespace in the application code. CSS and Markdown are excluded
# below because they already have owners.

# ── Vendored engine code, never edited ───────────────────────────────────
# ARCHITECTURE.md §"Engine logic stays vendored". These are compiler output
# from Marinara-Engine, carrying its 4-space indent. Formatting them would
# make every future re-vendor a conflict, and the diff would read as ours.
src/lib/lorebook-keyword-matching.js
src/lib/regex-safety.js
src/copy/vendor/

# ── CSS: stylelint owns it ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# `npm run csslint`, plus typescale.mjs, specificity.mjs and deadcss.mjs, all
# read these files already. Prettier would add nothing and cost a great deal:
# the token tables are hand-aligned one-liners
#
#   .type-thread       { --tc: var(--type-thread); }
#
# and Prettier gives every one of them three lines. Measured over src/styles
# alone that is memory.css going from 451 lines to 1,779 — a design-system
# reference that is read as a table, reformatted into something that is not.
*.css

# ── Markdown: Vale owns it ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# `npm run prosecheck`. Prettier does not reflow prose at the default
# proseWrap, but it does rewrite *emphasis* to _emphasis_ across every
# document — 23 files and roughly 500 lines of churn that changes no rendered
# output, in exactly the hand-formatted rationale blocks BACKLOG.md called out.
*.md

# ── Generated baselines ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Written by verify.mjs, typescale.mjs, deadcss.mjs and the CSS collision
# check. Formatting them means the next regeneration reverts the formatting
# and `format:check` fails, forever.
design/*-baseline.json

# ── Design surfaces that are not application source ──────────────────────
# The mockups are hand-written specimen pages kept close to what Luma was
# shown; kit.css is Tailwind output.
public/mockups/

# Lockfile: npm owns its formatting.
package-lock.json
